From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:57:29 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0307): release held input once the peer goes silent

AC-41, review follow-up to 0304. 0304 releases held keys and buttons when
the connection ends, but on a pulled cable the host only ends it at its
30 s receive timeout. The controller answers the host's TestDelay every
second, so after 3 s without any peer message the connection now asks
its input thread to release whatever it holds (idempotent; a peer that
comes back simply presses again). Release on teardown stays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
